 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nAccount and schedules the change for the date specified. Using the correspondence for master data changes he informs the\ntenant about the change planned in the system.\n\nContract Account and Contract Special Features for IS-U\n\nThis documentation section contains information about enhancements and variations from the FI-CA contract account and\ncontract, which apply specifically to SAP Utilities (IS-U).\n\nContracts (IS-U)\n\nDefinition\n\nContracts in IS-U.\n\nUse\n\nContracts represent the entities that are billed. You can bill one or more contracts together using a contract account.\n\nStructure\n\nYou can divide the data from contracts into three categories:\n\ne General data\ne Data relevant to billing (business)\n\ne Data regarding move-in and move-out.\n\nIntegration\n\nContracts are linked to installations in |S-U; these installations contain technical data with regard to billing. In the case of a move-\nout, the installation remains and the contract is ended. In the case of the next move-in, a new contract is created and linked to the\ninstallation. Only one contract can ever be assigned to an installation at any one time.\n\nControlling Specifications in Contract Accounts (IS-U)\n\nUse\n\nThere are a number of attributes in the contract account that are specific to IS-U. These can be divided into various areas:\n\nGeneral data, such as:\n\ne Indicator for additional bill\ne Transaction currency\n\ne Terms of payment\n\nA AnRnrniimt planer\n",
